> what is the range of x squared for a signed byte x?
  ucas: it(x: i8) = x^2
  ucas: range it
range of it -> i8:
  -127..121   (44 distinct values)
  values: -127, -124, -119, -112..-111, -103, -95, -92, -87, -79, -71, -63, -60, -55, -47, -39, -31, -28, -23, -15, -7, 0..1, 4, 9, 16..17, ...
  fits in i8
  over all 256 points of the domain
> what is pi to 10 decimal places?
  sorry: I didn't follow "to 10 decimal places"
> simplify x plus x
  ucas: simplify x + x
simplify x + x
  = 2x
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
> what is the derivative of x cubed?
  ucas: it(x) = x^3
  ucas: diff it
d/dx it = 3x^2
  holds for every real x
  check: matches central differences at 201 points (max relative difference 2e-15)
> factor x squared minus one
  ucas: factor x^2 - 1
factor x^2 - 1
  = (x - 1)*(x + 1)
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
  (factors are irreducible over the rationals)
> what is log of x
  note: "log" without a base: read as the natural log, ln, not log base 2 or log base 10 (say "natural log", "log base 2" or "log base 10", or "assume log means base 2")
  ucas: it(x) = log(x)
  ucas: show it
it(x: real) = log(x)
  -> real
> what is the square root of 16
  ucas: sqrt(16)
4
> what is the range of x squared for an unsigned byte x?
  ucas: it(x: u8) = x^2
  ucas: range it
range of it -> u8:
  0..249   (44 distinct values)
  values: 0..1, 4, 9, 16..17, 25, 33, 36, 41, 49, 57, 64..65, 68, 73, 81, 89, 97, 100, 105, 113, 121, 129, 132, 137, 144..145, ...
  fits in u8
  over all 256 points of the domain
